00:49:57.400 --> 00:50:02.740
each packet of data that is
being published to MQTT broker.

00:50:02.740 --> 00:50:05.090
And then when that
successfully happens,

00:50:05.090 --> 00:50:07.750
as we will not have
the luck to see today,

00:50:07.750 --> 00:50:11.060
you will actually see on your
screens, on your browser,

00:50:11.060 --> 00:50:15.260
you will see the blue line
connecting all the way through.

00:50:15.260 --> 00:50:17.410
And the page,
actually dynamically,

00:50:17.410 --> 00:50:21.730
instantaneously will show you
the graph with the two sensors'

00:50:21.730 --> 00:50:22.480
data.

00:50:22.480 --> 00:50:25.560
So the temperature and the
light sensor on this board.

00:50:25.560 --> 00:50:29.620
And it will be immediately
animated on your screen.

00:50:29.620 --> 00:50:33.880
How good would this be if
it was just a board and just

00:50:33.880 --> 00:50:36.340
this part of the experience?

00:50:36.340 --> 00:50:38.680
You know, the goal
here is not only

00:50:38.680 --> 00:50:43.030
to give you a five or sub 30
seconds, that's what we claim,

00:50:43.030 --> 00:50:45.190
experience and connection
to the Google Cloud.

00:50:45.190 --> 00:50:48.850
But after that, you will
want to change the sensors

00:50:48.850 --> 00:50:51.360
and apply your own
specific sensor.

00:50:51.360 --> 00:50:54.880
So you will want to write your
own firmware inside the board,

00:50:54.880 --> 00:50:57.040
inside the microcontroller
on this board.

00:50:57.040 --> 00:50:59.256
And just for you, if
you're not familiar

00:50:59.256 --> 00:51:00.880
with this particular
brand of products,

00:51:00.880 --> 00:51:02.770
you might have heard
that the AVR that

00:51:02.770 --> 00:51:05.290
is the microcontroller
shown here

00:51:05.290 --> 00:51:07.780
is the one that is
inside the Arduinos.

00:51:07.780 --> 00:51:12.550
So most students today coming
out of schools and university

00:51:12.550 --> 00:51:14.770
and out of--

00:51:14.770 --> 00:51:17.645
the hobbyists community are
very familiar with that.

00:51:17.645 --> 00:51:19.270
And so, they will
want to play with it.

00:51:19.270 --> 00:51:22.570
And so, professional and
nonprofessional developers

00:51:22.570 --> 00:51:24.730
actually will find a
solution that we prepared

00:51:24.730 --> 00:51:28.270
for them, which is,
as Kerry mentioned

00:51:28.270 --> 00:51:32.350
before, we have a rapid
development toolset that

00:51:32.350 --> 00:51:39.180
is composed of two pieces
of software, MCC and START.

00:51:39.180 --> 00:51:42.280
One for the PIC devices and
one for the AVR devices.

00:51:42.280 --> 00:51:44.890
And with those, literally
with a click of the mouse

00:51:44.890 --> 00:51:46.150
you will be able to see--

00:51:49.390 --> 00:51:52.190
let me just scroll
to the correct page.

00:51:52.190 --> 00:51:54.910
So this is START
for the AVR devices.

00:51:54.910 --> 00:51:56.650
And here you see
the blocks composing

00:51:56.650 --> 00:51:58.480
the project that
is actually running

00:51:58.480 --> 00:52:00.520
on this board in
this very moment.

00:52:00.520 --> 00:52:03.170
And this is available
in your browser.

00:52:03.170 --> 00:52:04.890
So you will do all
your reconfiguration

00:52:04.890 --> 00:52:08.840
of the device on the fly,
clicking on each block,

00:52:08.840 --> 00:52:10.030
changing the configuration.

00:52:10.030 --> 00:52:11.830
You see the
cryptoauthentication block.

00:52:11.830 --> 00:52:13.810
That's what controls the ECC608.

00:52:13.810 --> 00:52:17.750
So all the software is wrapped
in there and templated by that.

00:52:17.750 --> 00:52:21.670
And so, the MQTT IoT block
that you see there in blue

00:52:21.670 --> 00:52:25.060
is the block that wraps
the entire communication

00:52:25.060 --> 00:52:28.150
infrastructure, everything that
is needed to access the WINC

00:52:28.150 --> 00:52:31.210
device, the Wi-Fi chip.

00:52:31.210 --> 00:52:35.260
And the part on the left where
you see scheduler, ADC user,

00:52:35.260 --> 00:52:38.900
the embedded developers among
you will recognize those names.

00:52:38.900 --> 00:52:41.350
Those are the acronyms of
the individual peripherals

00:52:41.350 --> 00:52:42.720
inside the chip.

00:52:42.720 --> 00:52:45.730
And so, again, you can go there
and configure them, and select

00:52:45.730 --> 00:52:48.970
them, and make them read
temperature, read humidity,

00:52:48.970 --> 00:52:51.820
read whatever other
entity you want to read.

00:52:51.820 --> 00:52:54.430
And so, you can create
a complete solution

00:52:54.430 --> 00:52:56.080
with a few clicks of your mouse.

00:52:56.080 --> 00:52:58.480
And then hit up
there Export Project,

00:52:58.480 --> 00:53:02.020
and just hit the Build
button on your [? ID. ?]

00:53:02.020 --> 00:53:07.100
And with this, I will give
back to the mic to Zollie.

00:53:07.100 --> 00:53:10.150
ZOLTAN ARATO: Yeah, and
please stay on stage.

00:53:10.150 --> 00:53:12.790
Just very quickly because
we are running out of time,

00:53:12.790 --> 00:53:16.711
can we please go back
to the presentation?

00:53:16.711 --> 00:53:17.490
Thank you.

00:53:17.490 --> 00:53:24.870
So just a very quick summary
of the whole presentation.

00:53:24.870 --> 00:53:26.300
So as I said,
there are two sides

00:53:26.300 --> 00:53:31.040
of providing end-to-end
security, hardware,

00:53:31.040 --> 00:53:33.740
software cloud.

00:53:33.740 --> 00:53:36.560
Strong IoT security
uses a secure chip.

00:53:36.560 --> 00:53:40.010
And then ease of design
with the turnkey MCU.

00:53:40.010 --> 00:53:45.170
So you've seen that 8-bit
MCU which is brand new.

00:53:45.170 --> 00:53:48.830
And then when it comes to the
cloud, simple connection which

00:53:48.830 --> 00:53:51.190
we were unfortunately
unable to demonstrate.

00:53:51.190 --> 00:53:53.030
But it is simple, believe me.

00:53:53.030 --> 00:53:54.350
I saw it.

00:53:54.350 --> 00:53:58.490
And built in, so built
into these devices.

00:53:58.490 --> 00:54:00.960
They can connect to
the cloud and scale.

00:54:00.960 --> 00:54:05.900
So Cloud IoT provides
scaling on demand and also

00:54:05.900 --> 00:54:11.360
actionable insights using
the other Google Cloud tools

00:54:11.360 --> 00:54:13.350
and services.

00:54:13.350 --> 00:54:17.010
And with that, we would like
to conclude our presentation.

00:54:17.010 --> 00:54:17.960
Thanks for attending.

